{
 "about": [
  "Two signed values on one cell never replace each other. They relate by the cell's order:",
  "equal values are one encounter, the narrower value stands over the wider one, and",
  "incomparable values all stand as a fork that keeps both signers.",
  "",
  "It got its own file because the first render of the owner's ledger kept the last line of",
  "each claim key and hid the rest by file order — ten keys on 2026-09-17, six of them",
  "re-signs that moved `needs` without withdrawing the old line.",
  "",
  "`standing` lists the member indices of every class left standing; an encounter keeps",
  "every member, because no signature is overwritten."
 ],
